  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a tangent to the ellipse $\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+\\frac{y^{2}}{1}=1$ at any point. The locus of the midpoint of the portion intercepted between the axes is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "H1EY1",
      "text": "$\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+\\frac{y^{2}}{4}=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LJlfQ",
      "text": "$\\frac{x^{2}}{4}+\\frac{y^{2}}{2}=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hR2V9",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3 x^{2}}+\\frac{1}{4 y^{2}}=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "evra5",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2 x^{2}}+\\frac{1}{4 y^{2}}=1$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\nTangent at $\\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{x}_{1}, \\mathrm{y}_{1}\\right)$\r\n$\\frac{x x_{1}}{2}+\\frac{y y_{1}}{1}=1$\r\nLet mid point of intercept be $\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{h}, \\mathrm{k})$\r\n$\\mathrm{h}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{x}_{1}}, \\mathrm{k}=\\frac{1}{2 \\mathrm{y}_{1}}$ or $\\mathrm{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~h}}, \\mathrm{y}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2 \\mathrm{k}}$\r\nlocus is $\\frac{1}{2 x^{2}}+\\frac{1}{4 y^{2}}=1$",
    "image": null
  },
